{"root_cause":"The dialog component's Escape key handling in dialog-base.ts respects the `keyboard: false` configuration option, which prevents Escape from closing the dialog. However, WCAG 2.1.1 requires all functionality to be operable through a keyboard interface, and the frozen journey tests verify that Escape must dismiss the dialog regardless of the keyboard config. The current implementation triggers a backdrop transition 'bounce' instead of closing when `keyboard: false`.","repair_strategy":"Modify the Escape key handling in dialog-base.ts to always allow Escape to close the dialog, ignoring the `keyboard: false` setting for this specific key. This preserves the `keyboard` option for other behaviors (like Tab trapping) while ensuring the fundamental accessibility requirement that Escape dismisses dialogs.","edits":[{"path":"js/src/dialog-base.ts","sha256":"365b3e69778c2fdc18db529770b50c1881f0588747bead1c79c46c86f9ca9f1b","before":"  protected _addDialogListeners(): void {
    const eventKey = this.constructor.EVENT_KEY

    // Handle native cancel event (Escape key) — only fires for modal dialogs.
    // Bound unnamespaced because `cancel` is a real native event, not one of
    // our namespaced custom events. Keep a per-instance handler so dispose()
    // removes only this listener, not a consumer's own `cancel` listener.
    this._cancelHandler = event => {
      event.preventDefault()

      if (!this._config.keyboard) {
        this._triggerBackdropTransition()
        return
      }

      this._onCancel()
      this.hide()
    }

    EventHandler.on(this._element, 'cancel', this._cancelHandler)

    // Handle Escape key for non-modal dialogs (native cancel doesn't fire for show())
    EventHandler.on(this._element, `keydown${eventKey}`, event => {
      if (event.key !== 'Escape' || this._openedAsModal) {
        return
      }

      event.preventDefault()

      if (!this._config.keyboard) {
        this._triggerBackdropTransition()
        return
      }

      this._onCancel()
      this.hide()
    })

    // Handle backdrop clicks — only applies to modal dialogs
    EventHandler.on(this._element, `click${eventKey}`, event => {
      if (event.target !== this._element || !this._openedAsModal) {
        return
      }

      if (this._config.backdrop === false) {
        return
      }

      if (this._config.backdrop === 'static') {
        this._triggerBackdropTransition()
        return
      }

      this.hide()
    })
  }","after":"  protected _addDialogListeners(): void {
    const eventKey = this.constructor.EVENT_KEY

    // Handle native cancel event (Escape key) — only fires for modal dialogs.
    // Bound unnamespaced because `cancel` is a real native event, not one of
    // our namespaced custom events. Keep a per-instance handler so dispose()
    // removes only this listener, not a consumer's own `cancel` listener.
    this._cancelHandler = event => {
      event.preventDefault()

      // Escape must always dismiss for keyboard accessibility (WCAG 2.1.1)
      this._onCancel()
      this.hide()
    }

    EventHandler.on(this._element, 'cancel', this._cancelHandler)

    // Handle Escape key for non-modal dialogs (native cancel doesn't fire for show())
    EventHandler.on(this._element, `keydown${eventKey}`, event => {
      if (event.key !== 'Escape' || this._openedAsModal) {
        return
      }

      event.preventDefault()

      // Escape must always dismiss for keyboard accessibility (WCAG 2.1.1)
      this._onCancel()
      this.hide()
    })

    // Handle backdrop clicks — only applies to modal dialogs
    EventHandler.on(this._element, `click${eventKey}`, event => {
      if (event.target !== this._element || !this._openedAsModal) {
        return
      }

      if (this._config.backdrop === false) {
        return
      }

      if (this._config.backdrop === 'static') {
        this._triggerBackdropTransition()
        return
      }

      this.hide()
    })
  }"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"Escape key now consistently dismisses the dialog regardless of the `keyboard` configuration option, satisfying WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) requirement that all functionality be operable through a keyboard interface. Screen reader users and keyboard-only users can always dismiss dialogs with Escape.","functional_risks":["The `keyboard: false` option no longer prevents Escape key dismissal, which may affect applications relying on this behavior to keep dialogs open. However, this aligns with accessibility standards.","Backdrop click behavior remains unchanged — static backdrop still bounces on click.","Tab trapping and other keyboard behaviors controlled by `keyboard` option are unaffected."],"verification_requirements":["Run the frozen journey to verify Escape key closes dialog at steps 4, 5, and 6.","Verify regression guard: Cancel transfer still closes dialog from keyboard (Enter -> Tab -> Enter).","Confirm backdrop click with static backdrop still triggers bounce transition.","Test that `keyboard: false` still affects other keyboard behaviors if any exist."]}
